---
// The cross-document worked example, lifted out of /creator/studio/cross-document
// on 2026-08-25 so it could move with the form into the Ask tab of /audit.
// Unchanged content: every quote in it has already been through the verbatim
// quote gate against its source page, and a sample invented for prettiness
// would be the exact sin this publication exists to catch.
import WorkedExampleTour, { BODY_ID, COLLAPSED_KEY } from './WorkedExampleTour';
---
    <section class="mb-10 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-surface overflow-hidden">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-hairline" data-xdoc-example-header>
        <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted m-0">
          Worked example · three documents on nuclear costings
        </p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-muted m-0">prepared, not live</p>
          <WorkedExampleTour client:load />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 space-y-4" id={BODY_ID}>

        <p class="font-serif text-lg text-ink-strong leading-snug m-0" data-tour-anchor="xdoc-question">
          Is a nuclear-inclusive grid cheaper for Australia than renewables-only?
        </p>

        <div data-tour-anchor="xdoc-positions">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted mb-1.5">Where each document lands</p>
          <div class="space-y-1.5">
            <div class="rounded border border-hairline bg-paper px-3 py-2">
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted m-0">Doc A · Frontier Economics</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink m-0 leading-snug">A nuclear-inclusive grid is 25 per cent cheaper than the renewables-only pathway.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded border border-hairline bg-paper px-3 py-2">
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted m-0">Doc B · CSIRO GenCost</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink m-0 leading-snug">Prices each technology on its own, and says itself that it cannot compare whole pathways.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded border border-hairline bg-paper px-3 py-2">
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted m-0">Doc C · Grattan Institute</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink m-0 leading-snug">The case to switch from renewables to nuclear has not been made.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted mb-1.5">The premises they actually contest</p>

          <div class="rounded border border-hairline bg-paper px-3 py-2.5 mb-1.5" data-tour-anchor="xdoc-premise-1">
            <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted m-0">Premise 1</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink m-0 leading-snug">Reactors would run about 90 per cent of the time.</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1 mb-2 leading-snug">Doc A's cost advantage needs it. Doc B prices a range far below it.</p>
            <div class="border-t border-dashed border-hairline pt-2 space-y-2">
              <div>
                <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-ink-strong m-0">Contests · Doc B</p>
                {/* No quotation marks here on purpose: GenCost's range is
                    reported in the briefing's own words, not as a verbatim
                    passage, and quotation marks are a promise this page
                    must never make lightly. */}
                <p class="text-xs text-ink border-l-2 border-hairline pl-2 m-0 leading-snug">GenCost's printed capacity-factor range is 53 to 89 per cent, taken from coal's own operating record.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-ink-strong m-0">Contests · Doc C</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink border-l-2 border-hairline pl-2 m-0 leading-snug">&ldquo;But assuming 90 per cent for a fleet of seven plants over a multi-decade lifetime looks overly optimistic.&rdquo;</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          {/* The verification footer sits inside this wrapper so the tour's
              last step can highlight premise 2 and the quote-gate promise as
              one block. The wrapper's space-y-4 reproduces the gap the
              footer used to get from the outer space-y-4; nothing moves
              visually and no wording changes. */}
          <div data-tour-anchor="xdoc-premise-2" class="space-y-4">
            <div class="rounded border border-hairline bg-paper px-3 py-2.5">
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted m-0">Premise 2</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink m-0 leading-snug">Nuclear arrives in time to matter for the coal exit.</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1 mb-2 leading-snug">If it cannot, the cost contest between the two grids never starts.</p>
              <div class="border-t border-dashed border-hairline pt-2">
                <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-ink-strong m-0">Contests · Doc C</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink border-l-2 border-hairline pl-2 m-0 leading-snug">&ldquo;Even on the most optimistic outlook, nuclear power won't be ready in time for the exit of Australia's coal-fired power stations.&rdquo; <span class="text-muted">- citing AEMO on timing</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs text-muted m-0 leading-relaxed">
              Everything in quotation marks above was checked word-for-word against its source
              page before publication; the rest is reported in our words. Your run gets the
              same treatment: quotes that cannot be verified in your documents are dropped,
              not softened.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* Pre-paint collapse for returning visitors. The island hydrates too
        late to stop the full example flashing open before it snaps shut, so
        this blocking script applies the stored collapsed state during parse.
        The island then takes over and keeps everything consistent. With
        JavaScript disabled this never runs and the example stays open. */}
    <script is:inline define:vars={{ collapsedKey: COLLAPSED_KEY, bodyId: BODY_ID }}>
      try {
        if (localStorage.getItem(collapsedKey) === '1') {
          var xdocBody = document.getElementById(bodyId);
          if (xdocBody) xdocBody.hidden = true;
          var xdocHeader = document.querySelector('[data-xdoc-example-header]');
          if (xdocHeader) xdocHeader.classList.remove('border-b');
        }
      } catch (e) { /* Storage unavailable: leave the example expanded. */ }
    </script>

